## Reviewer note on the three DG2-DG4 files
transformations/register-kit.ts:267-286 openWrite reloads the principal inside the transaction only with { atCommit: true }; without it, it
authorizes the request-start principal inside the same transaction. workflows/decisions.ts (the T04 PATCH core that T-DG5-BE-E3 extracted for
bulk editing), transformations/routes.ts and sustainment/handovers.ts keep their DG2-DG4 write paths, which were approved on that pattern
(D-073: the upload is the only route that waits on the client between authentication and commit). The P5 caller that reuses these cores,
forms/bulk.ts, re-checks the record type's write permission on the principal reloaded inside its transaction (bulk.ts header and
requireRecordWrite) before it calls any updater, so P5 adds no stale-authorization window. No finding.
